# Media copy (MC). The terminal has no printer and ignores every media copy function: there is no
# printer controller mode, so what a program sends after CSI 5 i is drawn like any text, and a
# stray CSI 5 i cannot silence the terminal.

test printer controller mode is not entered: the data is drawn
convention media copy is ignored, as modern terminals do; swallowing the data up to CSI 4 i (VT510 manual MC) would let a stray CSI 5 i silence the terminal, since a reset sent after it would be swallowed too
size 20 3
feed a\e[5ishown\r\nand \e[1;31mthis\e[0m\e[4ib
screen
|ashown|
|and thisb|
cursor 2,10

test a reset after CSI 5 i works
convention media copy is ignored, so RIS is read as usual
size 20 3
feed \e[5ihidden\ec
feed ab
screen
|ab|

test media copy functions print nothing and reply nothing
convention ECMA-48 MC (CSI 0 i), xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps i and CSI ? Ps i (print screen, print line, auto print on and off, print composed display, print all pages, the screen dumps) have no printer to go to; they are recognised and ignored
size 30 3
feed a\e[ib\e[0ic\e[4id\e[5ie\e[?1if\e[?4ig\e[?5ih\e[?10ii\e[?11ij\e[10ik\e[11il
screen
|abcdefghijkl|
reply none

test an answer is still given while media copy is asked for
convention nothing in media copy takes the answers away: DSR 15 says there is no printer
size 20 3
feed \e[5i\e[?15n\e[5n
reply \e[?13n\e[0n
